xt": "Opus 5.5's H4 lost 5.4 points, taking Black's lead from -0.5 to -5.9. The engine preferred E7. It was the first big swing of the game, and the position was never level again until the middle game."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "The 12k's J2 lost 8.0 points, moving the lead from -9.6 to -1.7 and handing Black a way back into the game. Opus 5.5 answered with F2, which lost 8.2 and put the lead at -9.8, so the chance lasted a single move."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "White's B5 lost 7.7 points and put Black ahead at +4.2. It is the only positive lead in the whole table. Opus 5.5 held it for exactly one move."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "Opus 5.5's B4 lost 7.3 points and swung the lead from +4.2 to -3.0. The engine wanted C7, high on the board. Black chose a low, local move, and the game got away from there."}, {"turn": 49, "text": "Opus 5.5 passed at -15.7, and the engine's choice was E2. The pass lost 10.1 points, the worst move of the game, and the lead dropped to -25.8. White took E2 on the next move, and Black could not recover."}]}, "audit": null}